    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0579" n="471" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg471"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Señor
                            Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to say in further reference to your
                    note of the 17th instant, that, as I learn by a telegram of 24th instant
                    referred to me by the Secretary of War on the 25th, the commanding officer of
                    the troops at San Antonio, Tex., is “of opinion that no armed party has crossed
                    into Mexico from the United States at any point in the vicinity of El Paso,” and
                    adds that “Col. Lazelle is now in control of matters at that point, from whom a
                    report is expected very soon as to the expediency of returning the cavalry to
                    its post.”</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin E. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
